{
  "description": "What only the store can decide, inside the commit: a replacement that does not exist, or lies in another scope, is ReplacementNotAllowed with no status; an ineligible one, with its status; an eligible one in the record's exact scope commits, the replacement stored on the event. Once A is superseded by B, superseding B by A is refused, because A is no longer eligible (the store's cycle walk would refuse it too). Retrying the committed supersession replays it, even once the replacement has moved on.",
